.FIRE WEATHER...
Issued at 152 PM PDT Mon Jul 27 2026

The elevated fire weather threat will persist across portions of
the area through mid-week. Overnight RH recovery will remain
moderate at locations at or above 2,000 feet with values around 40
to 50 percent. This will be particularly true across the
Mayacamas, highest peaks of the East Bay Hills, the Diablo Range,
Santa Cruz Mountains, Santa Lucia and Gabilan Ranges. Nocturnal
drying (rapid decrease in RH through the pre-dawn hours) may also
transpire which will increase the burn period or time in which
fire behavior may remain active. Afternoon RH will remain
critically dry with values between 20 and 40 percent, with far
southern portions of the interior Central Coast potentially seeing
min RH near 10 percent. Energy Release Components (ERC) are
projected to climb above the 95th percentile across the interior
Central Coast. Individuals across the area are advised to avoid
activities that may spark a fire. Fire crews are urged to exercise
extra caution when executing any prescribed burns, especially
where fuels, topography, and weather align.

